From 9b671490a6d282260ea4d4d9700276d7df8a9d24 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 18:32:27 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 04/31] Draw the message dialog and wait for the player's
 answer

sceUtilityMsgDialog answered every message at once without drawing it:
"OK" to a notice and "Yes" to every question, so a game could be told "yes"
to a save or overwrite prompt that nobody saw. The dialog is now drawn by
the interface over the running game (host/ui/message_dialog.*): the text
between two rules across the screen, OK for a notice or Yes and No for a
question, and the button hints. It stays VISIBLE until the player answers
with the pad, the keyboard or the mouse; the game reads a neutral pad
meanwhile. The answer (yes 1, no 2, back 3) goes into the parameter block.
A question opens on No when the game asks for that (option 0x100), and
back does nothing when the game turns cancelling off (0x80).

For tests and runs without a window, <prefix>_MSGDIALOG_ANSWERS=ok,no,...
answers the next dialogs in order. <prefix>_MSGDIALOG_INSTANT=1 is the old
instant behaviour except that questions are answered No, so nothing is ever
confirmed without a person. With no window and no scripted answer the
dialog waits and says so once. sceUtilityMsgDialogAbort is implemented.

Verified on Windows (Vulkan, AMD) with a game's autosave notice (options
0xA3): drawn, answered with the scripted virtual pad, and the game went on
to its title screen. Not verified: a yes/no question from a game, the error
mode's text, the mouse.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
